Started work via 3 parallel sub-agents (architecture, harsh AAA critic, physics/audio).

What I built: `index.html` — playable ThreeJS (v0.185.1 CDN) FPS: PointerLock look, WASD, arena collision, hitscan rifle with recoil/spread, tracer/muzzle flash, wave bots with chase AI, HUD (HP/ammo/kills/waves), procedural WebAudio gunshots. Verified: 10KB, 148 lines, present on disk.

Harsh-critic blind comparison vs COD (Black Ops 6/7 era): **0/15 PASS** — boxes vs 5-15M tris/frame, 256px canvas noise vs 4K PBR sets, 1 dir + hemi light vs RTGI + volumetrics, sine-bob vs mocap, oscillator pew vs Atmos, no netcode. Any gamer picks COD as AAA 99-100% in <500ms. Iterating procedurally cannot close this gap — it's ~2 orders of magnitude in texture/lighting information plus team/budget.

Concrete blocker: AAA COD parity requires ~3000-person team, $300M+ budget, photogrammetry/PBR 4K assets, mocap, GI/volumetrics, Atmos audio, server netcode — none available in 900s zero-asset browser session. Built best-effort playable prototype instead (index.html). Need user decision: licensed assets + team + months, or accept stylized indie scope.
